WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.087 --> 00:00:06.090
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:11.880
When I was two years old, my parents
noticed that I was not speaking.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.850
Quickly thereafter,
the doctors diagnosed me as deaf.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:22.020
For the next 12 years of my life,
I learned to speak.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.076
I spent many Sunday afternoons with
my mother on the bedroom carpet and

00:00:27.076 --> 00:00:29.480
she'd teach me words.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.145
We called these sessions words.

00:00:31.145 --> 00:00:38.178
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Basically,

00:00:38.178 --> 00:00:42.167
we would sit there and she would teach
me words and I would never forget this

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:45.400
story that my mother told me
about the first word I learned.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.860
It was the word up.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.700
She'd hold me in her arms and
she'd carry me up, and down the stairs.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:01:00.130
And she said to me, Caroline,
we're going up, up we go, up.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.288
All my mom's friends and family thought
she was crazy taking on this grand

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:08.830
project, but I want to say the word up.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:13.388
I see how she opened and closed her mouth,
up and closed with a pop.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.242
Finally, she would take my hand and
place it on her throat and

00:01:21.242 --> 00:01:26.070
I feel through the vibrations what
kind of sound she was trying to make.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:31.590
Finally, at the age 2.5,
I said the word back to her, up.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:37.900
When my mom heard these words, she was so
overjoyed to cry tears of happiness.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.560
I ask her, why did you teach me to speak
instead of teaching me sign language?

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.792
And she said, Caroline,

00:01:47.792 --> 00:01:50.820
it's because I wanted you to
connect with anyone in this world.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.910
I wanted you to introduce yourself and
say, hello.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.387
I want you to stand in front of
an audience and express yourself, and

00:01:57.387 --> 00:01:58.060
your ideas.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:05.190
Not a day goes by that I'm not grateful
for her teaching how to speak.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.880
The ability to connect with
anyone is such a privilege.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.310
I'm able to connect with anyone I can.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.871
And through the path of
learning how to speak,

00:02:14.871 --> 00:02:17.570
I've grown to learn about
the power of the word.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:24.270
I'm going to share a few short stories
with you about the power of the word.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.390
By the time I was in second grade, I had
slowly, but surely built up my vocabulary.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.750
However, it was a little
on the simple side.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.170
So I had a plan.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.828
After school,
I looked to read the dictionary.

00:02:37.828 --> 00:02:42.395
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It was a little tedious.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.270
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But I kept reading it.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:51.265
And then the next day I go into class and
I say, these very smart and

00:02:51.265 --> 00:02:55.740
complex words and
I thought I was so impressive.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.862
But the teacher would come over and
say Caroline,

00:02:58.862 --> 00:03:01.550
do you know why you're using these words?

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:02.840
Are they proud of you?

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.668
But you're not using them correctly.

00:03:05.668 --> 00:03:09.816
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I was embarrassed in the moment and

00:03:09.816 --> 00:03:11.940
it's funny now.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:18.720
But when I reflect back on it, I realize
sure, I used smart and complex words.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.800
But they didn't understand
what I was saying.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.892
And I have found time and
time again by using simple words,

00:03:24.892 --> 00:03:28.661
you can connect so
much more powerfully with anyone.

00:03:28.661 --> 00:03:32.285
By being simple, you are not dumbing down.

00:03:32.285 --> 00:03:35.761
You are being smarter with your time and
your words.

00:03:35.761 --> 00:03:38.438
Be powerful by being simple.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.229
Words allowed us to connect with others,

00:03:43.229 --> 00:03:46.290
but they also allow us
to imagine the future.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:51.162
About two years ago, I was skiing
down the slopes of New Zealand and

00:03:51.162 --> 00:03:53.250
I took a wrong turn and snap.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:58.110
I broke three out of four
of my knee ligaments.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:02.640
It was a very serious injury and
I immediately went into surgery.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.594
As I'm exiting the fog anesthesia, I see
this surgeon staring at me with a very

00:04:07.594 --> 00:04:12.110
serious face and she says, Caroline,
that was a very serious injury.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:16.742
You're going to have to work very hard
to walk againand I remember in that

00:04:16.742 --> 00:04:19.185
moment thinking I'm deaf already.

00:04:19.185 --> 00:04:24.152
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; My life

00:04:24.152 --> 00:04:29.186
is hard enough as it is.

00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:33.280
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But he was right, it was really hard.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.370
I would go to physical therapy
not make any progress.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:38.890
I was barely able to bend my knee.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:44.760
And slowly as the days went by,
as the weeks went by, fear crept into me.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.680
What if I never walk again?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.710
Finally, after a lot of resistance,
I met with a sports psychologist.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.508
Her name was Linda and
she would sit me down and she'd say, okay,

00:04:55.508 --> 00:04:56.900
let's close our eyes.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.280
Let's imagine that you're walking again.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.805
I'm a little bit of a skeptical person.

00:05:02.805 --> 00:05:05.455
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; So I'm like what is this exercise?

00:05:05.455 --> 00:05:08.230
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But she would walk me through.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.780
She'd say, okay,
let's imagine you sitting and getting up.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.730
Imagine you walking.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:17.730
Imagine you running,
feeling the grass on your ankles.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.550
So I did.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.519
Every day, I wake up and imagine
myself doing all of these things and

00:05:23.519 --> 00:05:25.830
what happened afterwards is amazing.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.850
I made rapid progress
in my physical therapy.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:33.780
I started walking again,
I was able to run and everyone was amazed.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:36.690
They didn't understand what was happening,
except me.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.510
I knew that a surgeon had healed
my body with the operation.

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:44.520
But Linda, the sport psychologist
had healed my body with words.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.550
I was able to visualize the future.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.950
She gave me a seed of a dream.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:55.260
When you think about how you use words,
you can either address the hardships.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.670
You had a really bad injury or
you can address the future and

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.110
address, and make up a vision.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.770
You can do it for
yourselves or for others.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:07.150
Be powerful by being inspirational.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.280
My last story is a love story.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:17.330
I love to write love letters.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:23.370
I have a whole stack of them on my desk,
but I've never really sent them.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.241
Because I didn't want to creep
out the person I was dating.

00:06:26.241 --> 00:06:31.133
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Until I finally met the one last

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:34.150
year who I wanted to send the letter to.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:39.310
I wrote it all in one go and
I sent it off, I didn't hear anything.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.440
I was terrified.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.015
&gt;&gt; But finally, I got response back and

00:06:45.015 --> 00:06:46.350
it was beautiful.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:51.010
And so in once said to me, being in love
feels like when you've lost everything,

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.225
but then it's been returned to you and
that's how I felt in that moment.

00:06:55.225 --> 00:07:00.686
[COUGH] A week later,
I'm at this person's house and

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:08.020
I see in the corner a waste basket and
it has all the drafts of my letter.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.560
So I decided to do what any
mature person would do.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.658
I respected this person's privacy.

00:07:13.658 --> 00:07:17.483
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; No.

00:07:17.483 --> 00:07:20.285
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I obviously read them all.

00:07:20.285 --> 00:07:24.755
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I'm embarrassed to say that, but

00:07:24.755 --> 00:07:29.480
I read them all and I had to learn
something really interesting.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.050
I'm reading through these drafts and
I notice something strange.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:36.950
There were all these really tender and
vulnerable words that were crossed out.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.102
But when I compared it to
the final letter I received,

00:07:40.102 --> 00:07:43.322
I noticed that my final letter
only had those tender and

00:07:43.322 --> 00:07:47.610
vulnerable words and that's where
the beauty of your letter came from.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.470
Be powerful by saying the lines
that you want to cross out.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.910
How do you measure a life?

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.800
You measure a life through words.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.360
Words are like seeds.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:07.010
When we say them,
they float through the air.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.980
They can remain a seed or
they can grow into something beautiful.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:15.370
Words can distance or they can connect.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.682
Words can harm or they can heal and

00:08:18.682 --> 00:08:23.780
words can transform lives
as they have done for me.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:29.866
All of you, as you go through this life,
think about how we

00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:34.832
use the power of the word to connect,
inspire and to lift up.

00:08:34.832 --> 00:08:38.871
Thank you.

00:08:38.871 --> 00:08:43.666
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:08:43.666 --> 00:08:48.149
[MUSIC]

